urned for nothing."},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Bind this CRM audience to the brand's merged PEOPLE matching a filter (e.g. {signedUp: true, replied: false} = product signups who never answered) instead of to an imported file, optionally scoped to a `segment` of the brand's own CRM (e.g. {segment: {dealStages: [{pipeline: 'Sales Pipeline', stage: 'Form Filled - No Appointment'}]}}). Requires provider 'crm'; exclusive with crmUploadId. A segment crm-service refuses is a 400 carrying its reason. Every serve passes the filter to crm-service (same brand-wide no-re-serve forever); each served person carries its phone when crm-service holds one. Validated against crm-service's serve-stats at creation (its counts become the audience's Size / Remaining). Immutable afterwards."},"offerId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"The offer this audience belongs to — a brand-service offer id. Scopes the audience to one distinct thing the brand sells; name uniqueness becomes per (org, brand, offer), so two offers of the same brand may each own an audience with the same name. Stored as-is: human-service defines no offer semantics and does not resolve the id (same as brandId). Omit to keep the brand-wide behaviour. Immutable afterwards."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"description":"Optional count snapshot the caller already obtained from /orgs/people/search/dry-run (apollo). St